{"judgments": [
  {
    "clause_id": "c001",
    "reasoning_cat1": "A plain identification of the two Consultants, the Company and an effective date keyed to the last signature; nothing in it carries two meanings, though it defines \"Consultants\" collectively without saying how the two share anything.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "Section 2.a then uses the singular \"Consultant\" and promises \"twenty-percent (20%) of the Profits,\" so the collective definition here leaves open whether 20% is per person or shared, a mild tension rather than a direct conflict.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.09,
    "prob_cat2": 0.13
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c002",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The recitals contain soft, undefined commitments — \"future consulting services to enhance the value for the sale\" upon request, and reliance on a Jasper Port \"scheduled for construction in 2023\" — whose content and effect are not fixed anywhere.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "The operative Sections 2.a and 2.b impose an unconditional 20% payment obligation with no requirement that any future services actually be rendered, so a party could argue the recital's services language is a condition the operative text omits (classic recital-versus-operative divergence), and Section 3's integration clause does nothing to resolve it.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.30,
    "prob_cat2": 0.50
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c003",
    "reasoning_cat1": "\"Profit\" is defined as total proceeds less \"reasonable expenses, holding costs and expenses relating to transactions regarding the property (i.e. donations, etc)\" — \"reasonable,\" \"holding costs,\" and an \"i.e. ... etc\" catch-all that misuses i.e. for e.g. leave the deductible categories genuinely unbounded (general-vs-specific and vagueness both).",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It must be read with Section 2.a, which measures the Consultants' 20% by this figure, and with Section 2.b, where the same 100-acre donation is treated as a benefit generating shared tax savings while the definition apparently treats donations as a profit-reducing expense — a real risk of internal incoherence.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.74,
    "prob_cat2": 0.40
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c004",
    "reasoning_cat1": "\"Consultant\" appears in the singular against the two-person defined term \"Consultants,\" and \"[u]pon sale of a portion or all\" leaves unclear how expenses and holding costs are allocated to a partial sale, so both the payee and the measure are arguable.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "Its operation depends entirely on the elastic Section 1 definition of \"Profit\" and on the preamble's collective definition of \"Consultants\"; the mismatch between them is the kind of point a court would have to resolve.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.42,
    "prob_cat2": 0.33
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c005",
    "reasoning_cat1": "\"Company or its principal may realize certain tax savings\" is permissive and indefinite, \"its principal\" is undefined, and payment is triggered \"once the risk of a federal or state tax audit has expired, which is expected to occur in October 2016\" — an expectation, not a fixed date — with a comma splice joining the two sentences.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "Read against Section 1, the donation is listed as an expense reducing \"Profit\" yet here generates a separate 20% entitlement, and the recital describes the donation as already completed with Consultants' assistance, leaving the timing and measure of this payment hard to harmonise.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.58,
    "prob_cat2": 0.36
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c006",
    "reasoning_cat1": "A short, conventional merger clause; the only soft edge is the limiting phrase \"in connection with Delta Bluffs,\" which confines its supersession effect but is not itself of two reasonable meanings.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It sits against the recitals in c002, which supply the only description of the consulting services and of the Jasper Port assumption; if one side relies on that background, the integration clause is the provision opposed to it, but the recitals are part of the same writing so the tension is limited.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.13,
    "prob_cat2": 0.20
  }
]}

